                <main class="mm-container">

                    <!-- Hero Section -->
                    <section class="mm-hero" id="overview">
                        <div class="mm-hero-eyebrow">Technical Reference &amp; Operator Manual</div>
                        <h1>Meta Migrator – Safe Odoo 19 Batch Migration</h1>
                        <p>
                            Meta Migrator automates the migration of custom models, fields, views, menus, security rules, and server actions
                            across separate Odoo instances via remote XML-RPC. With explicit top-down step sequencing, zero-write dry-run testing,
                            and specialized OWL 2 diff widgets, you can verify changes with complete confidence before applying them to target servers.
                        </p>
                        <div class="mm-hero-tags">
                            <span class="mm-tag">✓ Odoo 19.0+ Enterprise &amp; Community</span>
                            <span class="mm-tag">✓ Dry-Run Test with Zero Target Writes</span>
                            <span class="mm-tag">✓ 8 Specialized Object Diff Widgets</span>
                            <span class="mm-tag">✓ Multi-Pass Relational Dependency Solver</span>
                            <span class="mm-tag">✓ Non-Destructive XML View Merging</span>
                            <span class="mm-tag">✓ Cron Background Queue Execution</span>
                        </div>
                    </section>

                    <!-- Workflow Flowchart Section -->
                    <section class="mm-section" id="flowchart">
                        <div class="mm-section-header">
                            <span class="mm-step-num">0</span>
                            <h2>End-to-End Operational Workflow</h2>
                        </div>
                        <p>
                            The diagram below outlines the five operational milestones of a migration job. Follow this sequence to achieve safe,
                            repeatable migrations without circular dependency errors or schema corruption.
                        </p>
                        <div class="mm-figure">
                            <img src="/meta_migrator/static/description/images/workflow_flowchart.svg" alt="Meta Migrator Operational Flowchart"/>
                            <div class="mm-figure-caption">Figure 0.1: Five-Stage Migration Life Cycle – From Remote Endpoint Configuration to Verified Synchronization.</div>
                        </div>
                    </section>

                    <!-- Step 1: Connections -->
                    <section class="mm-section" id="step1-connections">
                        <div class="mm-section-header">
                            <span class="mm-step-num">1</span>
                            <h2>Configuring Remote Endpoints (Connections)</h2>
                        </div>
                        <p>
                            Before building a migration job, declare the source and target Odoo environments under
                            <strong>Meta Migrator &gt; Connections</strong>.
                        </p>

                        <h3>Input Fields Specification</h3>
                        <table class="mm-table">
                            <thead>
                                <tr>
                                    <th>Field Name</th>
                                    <th>Technical Name</th>
                                    <th>Example / Value</th>
                                    <th>Usage Guidance</th>
                                </tr>
                            </thead>
                            <tbody>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><strong>Connection Name</strong></td>
                                    <td><code>name</code></td>
                                    <td><code>Staging Instance (AWS)</code></td>
                                    <td>Human-readable label identifying the target instance environment.</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><strong>Server URL</strong></td>
                                    <td><code>url</code></td>
                                    <td><code>https://staging.mycompany.com</code></td>
                                    <td>Base HTTP/HTTPS address of the Odoo instance (without trailing slash).</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><strong>Database Name</strong></td>
                                    <td><code>db</code></td>
                                    <td><code>odoo19_staging</code></td>
                                    <td>Name of the target PostgreSQL database registered on the remote server.</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><strong>Login Username</strong></td>
                                    <td><code>username</code></td>
                                    <td><code>migration_admin</code></td>
                                    <td>Odoo user account with administrative permissions (Settings / System Admin).</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><strong>API Key / Password</strong></td>
                                    <td><code>password</code></td>
                                    <td><code>••••••••••••••••••••</code></td>
                                    <td>We strongly recommend generating an <strong>Odoo API Key</strong> under User Preferences &gt; Account Security.</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><strong>Timeout</strong></td>
                                    <td><code>timeout</code></td>
                                    <td><code>60</code> (seconds)</td>
                                    <td>Socket timeout for remote XML-RPC calls. Use 120s if transferring large views.</td>
                                </tr>
                            </tbody>
                        </table>

                        <h3>Verifying Connectivity</h3>
                        <p>
                            Always click the <span class="mm-btn-badge mm-btn-primary">Test Connection</span> button in the header. Meta Migrator connects
                            to <code>/xmlrpc/2/common</code> to authenticate and queries <code>ir.model</code> to confirm administrative access. A green notification
                            banner will confirm successful authentication with user ID and accessible model counts.
                        </p>

                        <div class="mm-figure">
                            <img src="/meta_migrator/static/description/images/step1_connection.png" alt="Odoo 19 Connection Setup Form"/>
                            <div class="mm-figure-caption">Figure 1.1: Connection Form – Verified remote authentication on target staging instance.</div>
                        </div>
                    </section>

                    <!-- Step 2: Migration Job & Steps -->
                    <section class="mm-section" id="step2-jobs">
                        <div class="mm-section-header">
                            <span class="mm-step-num">2</span>
                            <h2>Defining Migration Jobs &amp; Step Sequences</h2>
                        </div>
                        <p>
                            Navigate to <strong>Meta Migrator &gt; Jobs</strong> and click <strong>New</strong>. A job represents a reusable migration plan
                            consisting of discrete, re-orderable steps executed from top to bottom.
                        </p>

                        <h3>Execution Options</h3>
                        <table class="mm-table">
                            <thead>
                                <tr>
                                    <th>Option</th>
                                    <th>Technical Key</th>
                                    <th>Allowed Values</th>
                                    <th>Recommended Setting</th>
                                </tr>
                            </thead>
                            <tbody>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><strong>On Conflict</strong></td>
                                    <td><code>on_conflict</code></td>
                                    <td><code>overwrite</code> (Update if exists) | <code>skip</code> (Keep target as-is)</td>
                                    <td>Use <strong>Overwrite</strong> when deploying customizations from dev to staging/prod.</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><strong>Stop On Error</strong></td>
                                    <td><code>stop_on_error</code></td>
                                    <td><code>True</code> / <code>False</code></td>
                                    <td><strong>True</strong> (recommended). Halts execution immediately if a step fails, avoiding cascading schema inconsistencies.</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><strong>Run In Background</strong></td>
                                    <td><code>run_in_background</code></td>
                                    <td><code>True</code> / <code>False</code></td>
                                    <td>Set to <strong>True</strong> for jobs with &gt;50 fields or views. The task executes via an asynchronous cron job.</td>
                                </tr>
                            </tbody>
                        </table>

                        <h3>Supported Step Object Types</h3>
                        <table class="mm-table">
                            <thead>
                                <tr>
                                    <th>Object Type</th>
                                    <th>Permitted Actions</th>
                                    <th>Required Parameters</th>
                                    <th>Behavior Details</th>
                                </tr>
                            </thead>
                            <tbody>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><code>model</code></td>
                                    <td><code>create</code></td>
                                    <td><code>model_name</code>, optional <code>target_model_name</code></td>
                                    <td>Creates new model on target. If model already exists, Test marks it as unchanged without errors.</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><code>field</code></td>
                                    <td><code>create</code></td>
                                    <td><code>model_name</code>, optional <code>field_name</code></td>
                                    <td>Creates field with full attributes (relations, selections, compute, depends). If left blank, all manual fields are imported.</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><code>view</code></td>
                                    <td><code>create</code></td>
                                    <td><code>model_name</code>, <code>view_type</code> (list/form/search)</td>
                                    <td>Creates primary view on target matching source active view with lowest priority.</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><code>view</code></td>
                                    <td><code>update</code></td>
                                    <td><code>xml_id</code> (e.g. <code>sale.view_order_form</code>)</td>
                                    <td>Non-destructively appends new child elements/xpaths into target view's <code>&lt;data&gt;</code> tag. Target customizations are preserved.</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><code>server_action</code></td>
                                    <td><code>create</code> / <code>update</code></td>
                                    <td><code>xml_id</code></td>
                                    <td>Pushes Python server actions, model bindings, and security action states.</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><code>menu</code></td>
                                    <td><code>create</code></td>
                                    <td><code>model_name</code></td>
                                    <td>Synchronizes window actions, menus, and menu hierarchies for the model.</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><code>access_right</code></td>
                                    <td><code>create</code></td>
                                    <td><code>model_name</code></td>
                                    <td>Copies <code>ir.model.access</code> CRUD permissions, mapping security groups automatically.</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><code>record_rule</code></td>
                                    <td><code>create</code></td>
                                    <td><code>model_name</code></td>
                                    <td>Transfers domain force record rules and evaluation contexts.</td>
                                </tr>
                            </tbody>
                        </table>

                        <div class="mm-figure">
                            <img src="/meta_migrator/static/description/images/step2_job_form.png" alt="Odoo 19 Migration Job Form"/>
                            <div class="mm-figure-caption">Figure 2.1: Migration Job Form – Ordered steps list, execution options, and action buttons.</div>
                        </div>
                    </section>

                    <!-- Step 3: Wizard -->
                    <section class="mm-section" id="step3-wizard">
                        <div class="mm-section-header">
                            <span class="mm-step-num">3</span>
                            <h2>Accelerating Authoring with Field Generation Wizard</h2>
                        </div>
                        <p>
                            Instead of adding dozens of field steps manually one by one, use the automated field discovery assistant:
                        </p>
                        <ol style="margin-left: 24px; margin-bottom: 16px;">
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 8px;">Click the <span class="mm-btn-badge mm-btn-secondary">Generate field steps</span> button in the job form header.</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 8px;">Select the desired model from the dropdown (e.g., <code>res.partner</code> or your custom model).</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 8px;">The wizard queries the source system for all manual fields (<code>state='manual'</code>) and renders an interactive checklist.</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 8px;">Select all desired fields and click <span class="mm-btn-badge mm-btn-primary">Add Steps</span>. Steps are appended to the job with auto-incremented sequence numbers.</li>
                            <li>Click <span class="mm-btn-badge mm-btn-secondary">Sort by dependency</span> to ensure prerequisite models and reverse relations precede dependent computes.</li>
                        </ol>

                        <div class="mm-figure">
                            <img src="/meta_migrator/static/description/images/step3_wizard.png" alt="Generate Field Steps Wizard Modal"/>
                            <div class="mm-figure-caption">Figure 3.1: Generate Field Steps Wizard – One-click batch extraction of custom fields.</div>
                        </div>
                    </section>

                    <!-- Step 4: Test & Diff Inspection -->
                    <section class="mm-section" id="step4-diff">
                        <div class="mm-section-header">
                            <span class="mm-step-num">4</span>
                            <h2>Dry-Run Testing &amp; Specialized Diff Inspection</h2>
                        </div>
                        <p>
                            <strong>Never migrate blind.</strong> Before making any modification to your target instance, click the
                            <span class="mm-btn-badge mm-btn-secondary">Test</span> button in the header.
                        </p>

                        <div class="mm-alert mm-alert-success">
                            <strong>Zero-Write Guarantee:</strong> The <code>action_test()</code> process connects in strict read-only mode.
                            It constructs an in-memory virtual registry (<code>planned_models</code> and <code>planned_fields</code>) to validate downstream
                            dependencies, calculating exact planned changes without modifying a single row in the target database.
                        </div>

                        <h3>Exploring the 8 Specialized Change Widgets</h3>
                        <p>
                            After clicking Test, a new record is created under the <strong>Runs</strong> notebook tab. Open the run to view individual
                            granular change records. Each change record is rendered by an OWL 2 field widget optimized for its data type:
                        </p>
                        <table class="mm-table">
                            <thead>
                                <tr>
                                    <th>Widget Key</th>
                                    <th>Target Object</th>
                                    <th>Key Visual Capabilities</th>
                                </tr>
                            </thead>
                            <tbody>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><code>meta_model_create</code></td>
                                    <td>New Model</td>
                                    <td>Displays model identity card and interactive table of child fields with live text search, type filtering, error toggle, and column visibility picker.</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><code>meta_model_update</code></td>
                                    <td>Existing Model</td>
                                    <td>3-column comparison grid (<code>Target Current</code> | <code>→</code> | <code>Source Incoming</code>) highlighting state, name, and transient flag changes.</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><code>meta_field_create</code></td>
                                    <td>New Field</td>
                                    <td>Categorized property cards (Basic, Constraints, Relational parameters, Selection keys, Logic computes, Other) with colored pill badges.</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><code>meta_field_update</code></td>
                                    <td>Existing Field</td>
                                    <td>Summary chips for changed keys, 2-column <code>AttrTable</code> with word diffs, and amber warning alerts for high-risk modifications (type alterations, required flags).</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><code>meta_view_create</code></td>
                                    <td>New View</td>
                                    <td>View metadata header, interactive <code>CodeBlock</code> highlighting newly added tags, and a live XML element outline sidebar.</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><code>meta_view_update</code></td>
