                    <!-- Best Practices -->
                    <section class="mm-section">
                        <div class="mm-section-header">
                            <span class="mm-step-num">💡</span>
                            <h2>Operator Best Practices &amp; Safety Checklist</h2>
                        </div>
                        <ul style="margin-left: 24px; line-height: 1.8;">
                            <li><strong>Always Test Staging First:</strong> Never push directly to production without testing the exact same job against a staging replica. Because target connections are selected per run, you can run the exact same job against staging, verify it, and then switch the target connection to production.</li>
                            <li><strong>Group Contiguous Field Steps:</strong> When migrating models with cross-referencing fields (e.g. Model A points to Model B, which points back to Model A), keep all field steps in contiguous sequence. Meta Migrator automatically groups them into an atomic multi-pass field block.</li>
                            <li><strong>View Update vs View Create:</strong> Use <code>create</code> for standalone views you authored from scratch; use <code>update</code> with standard Odoo XML IDs (like <code>sale.view_order_form</code>) when adding fields or tabs into existing views.</li>
                            <li><strong>Preserve Workspace Cleanliness:</strong> Change records are immutable snapshots. If you revise your source definitions, simply trigger a new Test run to generate fresh diff records.</li>
                        </ul>
                    </section>

